    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Violence against women (VAW) is a major determinant in the assessment of a wo-men's mental health. Many interventions have addressed strategies to reduce VAW,however, little information is available regarding effectiveness in the local context,particularly the role of men in women's empowerment. In Pakistan, a qualitativeapproach was undertaken in all four of its provinces to describe the communityresidents', both men and women, perceptions regarding the acceptability of a pro-posed life skills building (LSB) intervention involving men's engagement with regardsto women's empowerment and VAW.  To read article click here",
